  "protocol_note": "Purposefully search development conditions favorable to Ours, with all six methods sharing each public condition and per-condition retuning of every exposed baseline defense parameter. Two development seeds only; the formal seed and official-test outcomes never guide search. Each public block gives four candidates to each tunable defense and one to each fixed algorithm, all evaluated for 150 rounds on both seeds and ten scenarios. TPE fits observed losses after default/random startup; this learns a surrogate over configurations, not globally optimal weights. K is chosen jointly with training/attack hyperparameters; every method is attacked from K+2 in that block. Only equal completed inner-search budgets contribute to the final selection; partial/operational failures and checkpoints are retained. The 48-hour budget covers active search execution and stops workers after saving a round, so checkpoint latency may cause an overrun. This may be insufficient to finish any eligible block on actual hardware; never substitute partial metrics. Formal training is outside this budget. Training split and official test have prior research history; new seeds do not make them unseen. Historical models, protocols and outputs remain separately reproducible."
